WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.500
A cry for help as coastlines of vulnerable island states vanish under rising sea levels…

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.000
A distress call as swathes of the ancient ice sheets of Greenland and the Antarctic melt away

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.000
and the Arctic sea ice diminishes rapidly.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:36.000
A white flag as our most emblematic coral reefs, Earth’s single biggest living structure succumb to bleaching.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.000
These are no longer warning shots. These are not signals but symptoms.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:52.000
Our ocean is suffering some of the most dramatic and damaging effects of climate change.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.500
Greenhouse gas emissions generated by human activity

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.500
are causing sea temperatures to rise faster than ever recorded,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.000
destabilising ecosystems and reducing biodiversity.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.800
These same emissions are changing our ocean’s very chemistry.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.800
Increased acidification caused by carbon dioxide

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.500
jeopardises whole species of marine life,

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.000
including plankton, the very basis of it all.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Absorbing up to 90% of excess greenhouse heat,

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.500
our ocean is doing more than its share to help regulate the Earth’s climate

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.500
and diminish the effects of climate change.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.000
Now it is our turn to act.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:51.000
If we do not, extreme weather conditions such as cyclones and tropical storms will only increase,

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:58.000
wreaking havoc in coastline communities and threatening to sweep away vulnerable traditional livelihoods.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.800
So, how will we fight climate change?

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.000
How will we mitigate its effects on us,

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.000
our islands,

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.200
our coasts

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.500
and our ocean?

